### Assets — upload, serve, delete
### Routes: /api/assets/*  (+ the static /uploads/* mirror)
###
### Uploads are multipart/form-data with a single `file` field. Supported types:
### JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP, SVG. Size limit 10MB. The server returns a generated
### name; serve and delete use the path under /assets returned at upload time.

@assetPath = images/REPLACE_WITH_GENERATED_NAME.png

### Upload an image
### REST Client reads the file relative to THIS .http file. Drop a sample image
### next to it (e.g. http/sample.png) or point the path at any local image.
# @name uploadAsset
POST {{apiUrl}}/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----SchistFormBoundary

------SchistFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./sample.png
------SchistFormBoundary--
# => 201 { "message": "Asset uploaded successfully", "asset": { "path": "/assets/images/...", ... } }

### Serve an uploaded asset via the API route
GET {{apiUrl}}/assets/{{assetPath}}
# => 200 binary file content

### Serve the same asset via the static mirror (served at the server root, not /api)
GET {{baseUrl}}/uploads/{{assetPath}}

### Delete an uploaded asset
DELETE {{apiUrl}}/assets/{{assetPath}}
# => 200 { "message": "Asset deleted successfully", "path": ... }

#############################################
### Error cases
#############################################

### Upload with no file field
POST {{apiUrl}}/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----SchistFormBoundary

------SchistFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="notfile"

oops
------SchistFormBoundary--

### Serve a missing asset
GET {{apiUrl}}/assets/images/does-not-exist.png
